FDWM's own: a small square in the top left corner of each tag holding
windows, in SchemeNorm's col_fg (the palette's ui_text), filled while the
focused window is on that tag and empty otherwise; a tag holding an urgent
window draws it inverted, like its label. It is upstream dwm's occupied-tag
marker, the same drw_rect() call: activetagindicatorbar had turned it into
an underline under every occupied tag, and import-edits had kept the
underline for the selected tag only, in the accent, which stays. Scratchpads
are on tags of their own past the nine, so they mark none. The man page
says so.

